  "verbalization": "The compound [(1S,3S,7S,8S,11S,12S,14S,15R,16R)-15-[(2S,3R)-3-hydroxy-6-methyl-5-methylidene-4-oxoheptan-2-yl]-7,12,16-trimethyl-6-oxo-14-pentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadec-4-enyl] acetate is identified as a target of multiple pathways leading to Phosphodiesterase 6C. This includes its interaction with HaCaT cells, which are known to be targets of both (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione and Melodinine D, both of which are linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, the compound is also associated with the CD276 antigen, which is a target of 6-O-Veratroylcatalpol, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways, possibly involving cell surface receptors or signaling cascades. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains uncertain.",
